WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.740
If agrin from the nerve switches on MuSK, then no nerve should mean no clusters.

2
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:09.780
Is that true?

3
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:15.773
Muscle cells grown in a dish, with no neurons at all, make small receptor clusters

4
00:00:15.773 --> 00:00:16.773
by themselves.

5
00:00:17.666 --> 00:00:19.346
But a dish is not an embryo.

6
00:00:20.346 --> 00:00:22.946
In an animal, a nerve might have marked the spot first.

7
00:00:23.966 --> 00:00:29.806
In 2001, two groups studied mouse embryos whose diaphragm receives no motor axons.

8
00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:33.416
The diaphragm is the muscle that drives breathing.

9
00:00:34.356 --> 00:00:38.496
They stained it with a toxin that labels the muscle's acetylcholine receptors.

10
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:43.390
If the nerve chooses where receptors gather, what should the stain show?

11
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.350
And if the muscle chooses?

12
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:55.953
A band of receptor clusters still formed across the middle of the muscle.

13
00:00:56.793 --> 00:00:58.713
That is where the nerve would normally arrive.

14
00:00:59.716 --> 00:01:04.476
Burden's group also found receptor RNA concentrated in the same band.

15
00:01:05.466 --> 00:01:08.766
The muscle had drawn a rough map of where junctions would go.

16
00:01:09.506 --> 00:01:10.646
It is called the prepattern.

17
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.220
What does the prepattern need?

18
00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.480
Remove one part at a time.

19
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:19.413
Embryos lacking agrin still build the early band.

20
00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:22.393
The nerve's signal is not needed to start.

21
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.703
Embryos lacking MuSK make receptors, but no band.

22
00:01:27.563 --> 00:01:30.203
So the muscle's own kinase is needed for the band.

23
00:01:31.166 --> 00:01:34.166
Without rapsyn, there is no band of clusters either.

24
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.840
So the muscle's own machinery is needed to start the band, and the nerve's signal is

25
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.980
not. The muscle proposes.

26
00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:44.533
The nerve still matters.

27
00:01:45.753 --> 00:01:48.253
Contact makes far more clustering and narrows the band.

28
00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:53.253
Without a nerve, the band was wider, and its clusters belonged to no terminal.

29
00:01:54.316 --> 00:01:55.856
Keep two statements apart.

30
00:01:56.756 --> 00:01:58.336
Clusters can form without a nerve.

31
00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:00.196
A synapse cannot.

32
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.390
Takeaway: the muscle draws a rough map by itself.

33
00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.850
The nerve's work is to edit it.
